---
description: Never leave expiring Figma MCP asset URLs in app source
alwaysApply: true
---

# Local assets only

`https://www.figma.com/api/mcp/asset/...` URLs expire in about 7 days and break icons in production.

When implementing Figma designs:

1. Download the asset bytes immediately into `src/assets/` (or `src/assets/figma/`).
2. Import the local file in React. Do not keep the remote Figma URL in JSX, CSS, or data objects.
3. Reuse an existing local icon if it already matches (logo, chevron, like, bookmark, person-plus).
4. After adding images, run `npm run lint` so `scripts/check-no-figma-urls.mjs` fails if a Figma MCP URL slipped in.

If a Figma export URL is already expired, recreate or copy a matching local SVG/PNG. Do not leave a dead URL.
